    "faq_story": {
      "type": "cro-faq-story",
      "blocks": {
        "question_story_1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Does it work with launch monitors?",
            "answer": "<p>Absolutely.</p><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.thenetreturn.com/collections/flightscope\" target=\"_blank\">FlightScope</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.thenetreturn.com/collections/foresight\" target=\"_blank\">Foresight</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.thenetreturn.com/collections/fullswing\" target=\"_blank\">Full Swing</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.thenetreturn.com/collections/garmin\" target=\"_blank\">Garmin</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.thenetreturn.com/collections/uneekor\" target=\"_blank\">Uneekor</a> </li><li>and more</li></ul><p>The frame clicks together. The net attaches with <strong>color</strong>‑coded straps. It’s designed so anyone can assemble it without frustration.And if you ever want to move it, it packs down just as easily.</p><p>If you can swing a club comfortably, you can almost always fit a Net Return.</p><p>It’s designed to work in:</p><ul><li>garages</li><li>spare rooms</li><li><strong>backyards</strong></li></ul>"
          }
        },
        "question_story_2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How long will it actually last?",
            "answer": "<p>Longer than anything else in its category.</p><p>The frame is made from <strong>commercial‑grade aluminium</strong>. The netting is UV‑treated, weather‑resistant, and designed to <strong>absorb ball speeds up to 250mph</strong>.</p><p>Most customers tell us the same thing:</p><p>“It feels like something I’ll own for life.”</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_story_3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is it actually easy to set up?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes.</p><p>Most golfers set it up in 5–10 minutes without tools.</p><p>The frame clicks together. The net connects with color coded push buttons. It’s designed so anyone can assemble it without frustration.</p><p>And if you ever want to move it, it packs down just as easily.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_story_4": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Will it fit in my space?",
            "answer": "<p>If you can swing a club comfortably, you can almost always fit a Net Return.</p><p>It’s designed to work in:</p><ul><li>garages</li><li>spare rooms</li><li>back gardens</li><li>studios</li><li>sheds</li><li>offices</li></ul><p>If you’re unsure, you’re always welcome to contact our team and speak to an expert.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_story_5": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": " Is it safe to use indoors?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes.</p><p>The Net Return is engineered to <strong>return the ball safely back to your feet</strong> every time. </p><p>No ricochets. No unpredictable rebounds. No damage to walls or ceilings.</p><p>This is one of the biggest reasons golfers choose it over cheaper alternatives.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_story_6": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": " Is it loud?",
            "answer": "<p>Surprisingly quiet. </p><p>The net absorbs the ball rather than slapping it back.</p><p>Most golfers say they can practice early in the morning or late at night without disturbing anyone.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_QPbecy": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can it handle real golf balls?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes — that’s exactly what it’s built for.</p><p>You can hit full‑speed drivers, wedges, and everything in between. </p><p>Indoors or outdoors.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_HBnBAw": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Why do so many pros use it?",
            "answer": "<p>Because it’s consistent.</p><p>Because it’s safe.</p><p>Because it lasts.</p><p>And because it gives you the same reliable feedback every single session.</p><p>When you’re working on your game, consistency matters.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
